{#
  The autonomous work block: **only a driver** sees it, under the driver box,
  because it governs what sits above it.

  A driver filling in the pre-analysis may be bringing work of their own. In that
  case the driver's share is not added to the price, and any discounts or links of
  **other** drivers no longer count: a project is brought in by one person only.

  The link goes to the showcase site's "Work with us" page in a new tab: whoever
  follows it is filling in a form, and in the same tab would lose their answers.

  The checkbox does nothing by itself: the CSS reads `#autonomous-work:checked`
  (the `:has()` rule in styles.css) and switches off the box above, bringing up the
  notice. No JavaScript, no round trip to the server.

  When the form comes back — the request was sent back for want of detail — the
  checkbox says how the project stands and is **locked**: that choice was made at
  the first submission and the second round does not read it again. A checkbox that
  can be moved without the moving being good for anything is worse than a locked
  one.
#}

{% macro render(work) %}
      <aside class="card driver-work" aria-labelledby="driver-work-title">
        <div class="card-head aside-head" id="driver-work-title">{{ t("preanalyst.driver_work.title") }}</div>
        <div class="driver-work-body">
          {%- if work.own_link %}
          <p class="notice notice-warn">{{ t("preanalyst.driver_work.own_link") }}</p>
          {%- endif %}
          <label class="choice{% if work.locked %} choice-locked{% endif %}" for="autonomous-work">
            <input type="checkbox" id="autonomous-work" name="autonomous_work" value="yes"
                   form="gate-form"
                   {{- " checked" if work.checked }}{{ " disabled" if work.locked }}>
            <span>{{ t("preanalyst.driver_work.checkbox") }}</span>
          </label>
          {%- if work.locked %}
          <p class="driver-work-hint">{{ t("preanalyst.driver_work.locked") }}</p>
          {%- endif %}
          <p class="driver-work-hint">{{ t("preanalyst.driver_work.hint") }}</p>
          <p class="driver-work-hint">
            <a href="{{ work.more_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ t("preanalyst.driver_work.more") }}</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>
{%- endmacro %}
